WEBVTT

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:10.440
<b>The Boy from the West and the Knight of the Blue Storm</b>

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.100
You're up.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.560
Good morning.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.570
What's all this?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:35.660
You seemed cold, so
 I thought I'd warm you up.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.630
Thank you.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.210
They're a little heavy, though.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.250
Oh, sorry.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.470
Thanks.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.110
How do you feel?

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.010
Well...

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.130
She's still cold.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.360
Yeah...

00:00:53.770 --> 00:01:00.460
The cause of your malaise is still 
roaming about, so I'd expect so.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.380
Right.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:16.420
Let's find its master soon and 
send it back to the Wild Hunt.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.690
Once we can find their master, they'll stop 
wandering and return to where they belong.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.300
Your chills ought to go away, too.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.720
Let's get it over with, then.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.140
If you're cold, so am I.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.620
You're right.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.060
But, first...

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.270
Stare...

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.530
Shall we have breakfast?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.410
Have you seen my hair tie?

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.300
I'm sure you can buy one at 
the shop in the hospital.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.040
It's so far from the nurses' station, though.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:03.920
Are you not hungry?

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.770
Oh, no, you're really cold.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.270
Are you feeling ill?

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.230
I'm fine, jeez.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.550
What should I do?

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.340
Hopefully I can make a call during work.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.680
You don't have to!

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.530
I'm going to be working at home today.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.070
I'll call if anything happens.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.220
Thanks.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.480
Good.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.110
Morning.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.250
Sorry I couldn't get out here sooner.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.990
You must be hungry.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.940
Do you not eat human food?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.950
I get the strange feeling that I shouldn't.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.840
Okay.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.890
In that case, let's head out!

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.080
We'll find where you need to go for sure.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.990
I'm sure this rock will help us, too.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.010
Isn't that awesome?

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.550
I even have figures.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.240
Look!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.460
This horse is the knight's best friend.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.150
And this is the really evil wizard!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.670
"Foolish humans, feel 
the wrath of my flame!"

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.100
And then, he spews blue flames from here!

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.020
And then...

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.400
You think this is childish, huh?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.360
But, y'know...

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.760
I love this stuff.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.720
Ghosts, dragons...

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.560
Gates to other worlds deep in the forest...

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.910
Evil wizards and knights of light...

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.220
I used to have a friend 
who liked this stuff, too,

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.700
but I haven't seen him in a while, 
so I got a little excited.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.180
"Y-You evil wizard!"

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.450
Awesome.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.700
It won't be that easy!

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.290
Magic stone, give me power!

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.570
Y-You got me.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.240
No, no.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.730
You have to use your crystal shield to...

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.040
Hey, what's your name?

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.980
Let's think of one together, then.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.070
What would be a cool name for you?

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.850
Gigantes Messiah!

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.860
Gryphon Light.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.810
How about Earth, Fire and the Wind?

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:05.010
Then... how's Evan sound?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:06.960
Evan?

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.880
It's the name of a boy from
 an old French story.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.410
He's the protagonist in this book.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:26.800
Evan endures all kinds of trials so 
his dead friend makes it into Heaven.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.920
Isn't he great?

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.730
It's a story about friendship.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.390
Suits us perfectly, don't you think?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:33.820
Evan.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.430
My name is Evan?

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.860
Yeah, you're Evan.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.820
You should call me Gabe.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:43.870
Gabe.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.510
Let's go, Evan!

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.110
Okay.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.270
Now, then...

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:58.060
I wish we had some leads on the 
whereabouts of your master.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.830
Could you follow their scent?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.400
He says his nose is still messed up.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:08.500
Shall we check the area where 
the Wild Hunt showed up?

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.420
He says he got lost as he was wandering.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:17.460
Silky.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.950
What's this?

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.330
Okay, we'll be back.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.140
This way.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:39.060
Let's walk around.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:40.420
It's an adventure!

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.020
Are you okay?

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.660
I'm all right.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.970
Wow, though.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:15.420
I didn't think there'd be anything 
to see out in the boonies.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.410
I'm having a lot of fun today!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.140
It's all thanks to you.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.100
Me?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.780
Evan, look!

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:37.370
I've never seen anything 
like this in London.

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:40.640
Hey, have you seen this place before?

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.190
But I think it's been a while 
since I've been outside.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.970
Have you remembered something?

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.390
No, it's just a feeling.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.970
I never had a chance to go out.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:06.920
All I could do was watch 
as everything changed.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:12.020
I think I know the feeling.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.290
Look.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.090
You know how I'm always coughing?

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.490
This medicine helps stop it.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.610
I've always been sickly.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.640
The air wasn't very clean 
where I used to live.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.760
So I didn't get to play outside much.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.260
We're kind of alike, don't you think?

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:42.820
Alike?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:43.760
Yeah.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.160
We should hurry.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.840
It might be another storm.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:55.950
Let's go.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:56.680
Okay.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.720
Everyone says they saw 
the Wild Hunt run off.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:29.060
Yet no hint of the horse's master.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.300
My, that looks delicious.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.930
Your Majesty.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.990
Snacks baked by the silver child, yes?

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.310
I've heard about these.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.440
They say they're very delicious.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.890
I can't wait!

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.070
I see, I see.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.650
The lightning, huh?

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:01.380
Well, that's quite the pickle.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:05.630
They're causing Chise to fall ill.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:08.260
I'd like to resolve this immediately.

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:12.050
Head to the old battlefield.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.520
The first place of the Wild Hunt.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.280
You might learn something there.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.230
Thanks, Spriggan.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.220
I wish we could have spoken for longer.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.990
Let's head home and have tea!

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:31.990
Please? Please?!

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.520
Don't you need to have your 
medicine around your neck?

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.210
It's fine, I don't care.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.810
We'd both have something
 around our necks, then.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.970
All right, fine!

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.200
I just have to put it on, right?

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.060
Happy?

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.290
Okay, let's go.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:11.860
<i>What's happening?</i>

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.420
Are you okay?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.970
I-I'm fine.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.430
I j-just need some rest.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.070
Sorry.

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.140
I'm okay now.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:48.950
Sorry, could you toss that back?

00:12:58.180 --> 00:12:59.130
Thanks!

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.700
Hey, are you the new kid that just moved in?

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.350
Huh?

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.000
Are you by yourself?

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.570
Wanna play with us?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.220
Let's play soccer!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.400
We just need one more.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.630
Yeah!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.360
He can't run, though.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.710
That's an inhaler around your neck, isn't it?

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:28.080
My cousin has the same thing.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.070
We're gonna get in trouble 
if we try to make him run.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.400
Can't play, then, huh?

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:35.430
Bah. Let's go, guys.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:47.910
No...

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.050
No.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.800
No! I don't need it!

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.520
I don't need this thing!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.540
I'm done.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.650
I'm done with this scrubby little town.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.740
I was way better off in London.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:13.640
I don't need friends anymore.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:14.700
Yes, you do.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:20.340
Yes, you do.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.720
What is this thing?!

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.820
Let's run, Evan!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.210
Gabe...

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.490
Yes, you do.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.080
Yes, you do...

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.470
Yes, you do.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.140
U-Um...

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:31.860
Elias.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.410
Horse...

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:44.540
That's my horse.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.460
I'm sorry I lost you.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.190
Are you the people who brought him here?

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:39.940
You have my gratitude.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:41.510
I don't need thanks.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.690
Just hurry back to where you're from.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.560
I'd be more than happy to.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.530
Hold on!

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:49.880
What is this?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.490
What's going on?!

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.580
My friend...

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.830
I thank you, truly.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:56.750
Stop talking like that!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.110
You're Evan, aren't you?

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.990
That is the name you gave me, my friend.

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.650
I have no name.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.460
Only my duty.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.000
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.930
I can't blame you.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:14.180
I only just now remembered, myself.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.140
Thanks to you, my friend.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.390
Stop calling me that!

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.760
Just call me Gabe—

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.000
Are you okay?

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.900
What do you want?

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.550
And who's that creep?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.730
It seems they've taken quite 
an interest in you already.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:38.280
You'd better get away now, or you'll die.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.100
What are you...

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:40.980
Wait.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:43.880
I'll explain everything.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.370
Hear me out, okay?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.410
For their sake, too.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:03.180
So I want Evan to go back to his friends.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.850
I get that.

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:11.990
Thanks for listening to me.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.920
Good grief.

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:19.580
Elias.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.300
We have another problem.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.580
There's no sign of them anywhere.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.910
They aren't responding to the horn, either.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:31.380
We may want to wait for nightfall.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.470
I'll wait, too!

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:39.150
At least let me say goodbye if we 
can't see each other anymore.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:43.710
Elias, please.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:46.430
You're unbelievable.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:52.580
Gabriel, find me a stick.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.130
O-Okay.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.910
Put it there.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.700
Pardon me.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:02.860
Ow!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.890
Nettles in the shadow...

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.240
Ring of holly...

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:10.830
Fleeting bones, flesh of mud...

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.750
Step through thorn and thistle

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:19.580
to take your master's form 
until the promised time.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:29.260
Go home.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:41.000
We should head home, too, 
and wait for the night.

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.200
Sorry.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.500
We can't let Evan inside,
 but it's to protect you both.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.700
Gabriel, you can rest in this room here.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.750
I'll call you when dinner's ready.

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:14.140
It's so weird.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.520
We were together until just now.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.930
Now I can't even go near him.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:24.940
Hey, Evan...

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:28.850
Do you know what happens to 
the two friends in the story?

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:36.070
The angels are moved by Evan's friendship, 
and they take him to Heaven.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.300
And the two of them

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:43.600
live happily together forever.
